      "labels": [
        "p-primary-part"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "CommGroup.primaryComponent",
        "CommGroup.equivPrimeToComponentProdPrimaryComponent"
      ],
      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 50,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "If $M$ is a finite abelian group, $p$ is a prime, let $M(p)$ be the $p$-primary part of $M$, which is the $p$-Sylow subgroup of $M$, or the subgroup of $M$ consisting of elements whose order is power of $p$. By definition it is a subgroup of $M$, and is also canonically a quotient group of $M$."
    },
    {
      "id": "Zp-ext-Ln",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 11,
      "chapter": "arithmetic-of-p-extensions",
      "source": "content.tex",
      "line": 1464,
      "title": null,
      "labels": [
