      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 52,
      "proof_event": 53,
      "proof_chapter": "arithmetic-of-p-extensions",
      "proof_leanok": true,
      "text": "For each $n\\geq 0$ let $A_n:=\\Cl(K_n)(p)$ be the $p$-primary part of the class group $\\Cl(K_n)$, viewed as a quotient of $\\Cl(K_n)$."
    },
    {
      "id": "Zp-ext-L-inf",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 13,
      "chapter": "arithmetic-of-p-extensions",
      "source": "content.tex",
      "line": 1533,
      "title": null,
      "labels": [
        "Zp-ext-L-inf"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [],
      "leanok": false,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "Ln-K-Gal",
        "Ln-mono"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 57,
      "proof_event": 58,
      "proof_chapter": "arithmetic-of-p-extensions",
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "Let $L_\\infty:=\\bigcup_{n\\geq 0}L_n$. Note that each $L_n$ is Galois over $K$, so $L_\\infty/K$ is also Galois. Let $G=\\Gal(L_\\infty/K)$ and $X_\\infty=\\Gal(L_\\infty/K_\\infty)$."
    },
    {
      "id": "Zp-ext-totally-ramified",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 14,
      "chapter": "arithmetic-of-p-extensions",
      "source": "content.tex",
      "line": 1619,
      "title": null,
      "labels": [
        "Zp-ext-totally-ramified"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [],
      "leanok": false,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "Zp-ext-def"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 62,
      "proof_event": 63,
      "proof_chapter": "arithmetic-of-p-extensions",
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "A $\\BZ_p$-extension $K_\\infty/K$ is called totally ramified, if all primes which are ramified in $K_\\infty/K$ are totally ramified. More explicitly, for any prime of $K$, either it is unramified in $K_n/K$ for all $n$, or it is totally ramified in $K_n/K$ for all $n$."
    }
